WEBVTT

00:02.474 --> 00:03.998
&lt;i>Previously on Two and a Half Men:&lt;/i>

00:04.175 --> 00:05.403
Why were you in jail?

00:05.577 --> 00:07.602
I was forced to defend a lady's honor.

00:07.779 --> 00:10.646
- So I don't have to go back to jail?
- Not even a courtroom.

00:10.815 --> 00:15.252
We're having a nature ride and barbecue
for the kids Saturday. You should come.

00:15.420 --> 00:18.787
- That sounds wonderful. Doesn't it?
- You let her go without you?

00:18.957 --> 00:20.151
Why would I want to go?

00:20.325 --> 00:23.852
Maybe you didn't notice the way
my lawyer was looking at your fiancée.

00:24.029 --> 00:27.556
- What are you talking about?
- Or the way she looked at him.

00:28.233 --> 00:30.394
Charlie, that guy is everything you're not.

00:38.676 --> 00:41.304
- Where is she, Alan?
- Don't work yourself into a tizzy.

00:41.479 --> 00:46.382
A tizzy? I don't have tizzies.
Women have tizzies. You have tizzies.

00:47.619 --> 00:51.749
Me, I am outraged,
I am furious. I am... I am...

00:51.923 --> 00:53.220
Miffed?

00:53.391 --> 00:56.326
Do not complete my sentences
if you don't grasp the concept.

00:57.128 --> 00:59.858
- Sorry.
- She should've been home hours ago.

01:00.031 --> 01:03.125
- I'm sure there's a good explanation.
- And what would that be?

01:03.301 --> 01:07.260
Well, after the barbecue ended,
Chelsea stayed behind to help clean up...

01:07.439 --> 01:11.375
...then she and Brad got to talking about
all the things they have in common:

01:11.543 --> 01:14.205
Their love of horses, children.

01:14.379 --> 01:17.780
Probably just lost track of time
because he's so easy to talk to...

01:17.949 --> 01:20.782
...not to mention
how good-looking he is.

01:22.520 --> 01:24.545
Or she got diarrhea.

01:25.857 --> 01:29.384
Maybe she called.
Oh, look, there's two messages.

01:29.561 --> 01:31.426
&lt;i>Hi, I'm calling for Alan Harper.&lt;/i>

01:31.596 --> 01:32.858
&lt;i>This is Jenny from Malibu Day Spa.&lt;/i>

01:33.031 --> 01:36.000
&lt;i>Just wanted to confirm your
Saturday appointment for a bikini wax.&lt;/i>

01:39.104 --> 01:40.264
Bikini wax?

01:40.438 --> 01:44.169
I wear a European cut bathing suit,
I like to keep it tidy down there.

01:45.210 --> 01:47.371
Anyway, I'm sure
the next one is Chelsea.

01:47.545 --> 01:49.445
&lt;i>Hi, Mr. Harper. This is Jenny again.&lt;/i>

01:49.614 --> 01:53.414
&lt;i>Just a reminder, we can no longer
accept a personal check from you...&lt;/i>

01:53.585 --> 01:56.281
I should've just gone with her
to that charity thing.

01:56.454 --> 01:58.684
With effort, you wouldn't be
in this situation.

01:59.190 --> 02:01.590
I'll bet she knew I wouldn't go
when she asked me.

02:01.759 --> 02:05.490
I bet she was counting on me not going
so she could be alone with this Brad.

02:05.663 --> 02:09.690
- Chelsea would do something like that?
- Why not? That's what I'd do.

02:09.868 --> 02:11.836
I mean, hypothetically.

02:12.003 --> 02:14.995
If I were ever in that situation. Again.

02:16.241 --> 02:17.299
Right.

02:17.475 --> 02:19.966
Point is, I've been honest
through this whole thing.

02:20.145 --> 02:21.635
She's the one who's deceitful.

02:21.813 --> 02:25.010
She's nothing but a manipulative,
calculating, two-faced...

02:25.216 --> 02:28.344
- Hey, honey.
- Oh, hi, baby.

02:28.853 --> 02:30.980
- How was the party?
- It was great.

02:31.156 --> 02:35.149
There was 80 kids taking turns riding
a horse for the first time in their lives.

02:35.326 --> 02:38.887
- So, what, there was just one horse?
- No.

02:39.063 --> 02:41.930
Good, because that would've been
a tough day for the horse.

02:42.100 --> 02:45.160
Sorry I'm late, but after we got
the kids back on the buses...

02:45.336 --> 02:48.999
...a bunch of us helped clean up.
- Yeah, yeah, that's what I figured.

02:49.440 --> 02:52.307
Anyway, I'm beat. I wanna jump
in the shower and go to bed.

02:52.477 --> 02:53.739
Okay, I'll be right up.

02:53.912 --> 02:56.210
- Night, Alan.
- Night.

02:56.381 --> 02:58.076
Glad you had a good time.

02:58.249 --> 03:00.774
Well done.
You sublimated your anger...

03:00.952 --> 03:03.546
...and came from a place of love.
Took the high road.

03:03.721 --> 03:06.383
Really? Is that what you call it?
Because I call it...

03:06.558 --> 03:09.857
...a complete and total betrayal
of my testicles.

03:11.396 --> 03:15.196
If you'd done it as much as I had,
you'd call it the high road.

03:26.511 --> 03:30.811
Hey, Chels? So when you say
a bunch of you stayed to clean up...

03:30.982 --> 03:33.974
...how many are you talking about?
- I don't know, a couple.

03:34.786 --> 03:36.185
Uh-huh.

03:37.455 --> 03:39.821
You know, technically a couple is two.

03:39.991 --> 03:44.360
So there were two people in addition
to you and Brad, or just you and Brad?

03:44.529 --> 03:48.260
- What are you getting at?
- Nothing. Trying to get a head count.

03:48.666 --> 03:51.100
- You could've come with me, you know.
- I know.

03:51.269 --> 03:54.432
It'd be nice for us to do some things
together once in a while.

03:55.006 --> 03:56.530
We do plenty of things together.

03:56.708 --> 03:58.938
- Besides sex.
- Oh.

04:01.012 --> 04:03.173
When Brad's wife was alive
they played tennis.

04:03.348 --> 04:05.282
Probably what killed her.

04:05.850 --> 04:07.784
She was hit by a car.

04:09.053 --> 04:11.317
Maybe she was chasing a tennis ball.

04:13.191 --> 04:15.159
You know, like a dog.

04:16.895 --> 04:19.955
You throw it, they run after it.
Even if there's traffic.

04:21.633 --> 04:23.396
Goofy dogs.

04:32.877 --> 04:34.367
What the hell is that?

04:34.879 --> 04:38.144
Two guys in a cage
beating the snot out of each other.

04:38.316 --> 04:42.150
I can't believe I wasted so many years
watching cartoons.

04:42.320 --> 04:43.753
Turn it down.

04:43.922 --> 04:46.413
Aye, aye, Captain Douche.

04:46.858 --> 04:50.259
- What'd you say?
- Aye, aye, captain. I'll do that.

04:52.096 --> 04:54.326
Why are you on the couch?
You have a fight?

04:54.499 --> 04:56.023
No, we didn't have a fight.

04:56.200 --> 04:57.997
Were you farting in your sleep?

04:58.469 --> 05:00.733
- No.
- Did you screw up the sex?

05:01.739 --> 05:03.536
What the hell are you talking about?

05:03.708 --> 05:06.176
There's more than one way
to satisfy a woman.

05:06.678 --> 05:08.168
Really? Like what?

05:08.346 --> 05:11.213
I'm not sure. But I have some theories.

05:11.382 --> 05:12.713
Get out.

05:12.884 --> 05:14.351
Fine.

05:16.254 --> 05:18.848
We wouldn't have problems
if you put a TV in my room.

05:19.023 --> 05:22.083
We wouldn't have these problems
if I put a python in your room.

05:23.528 --> 05:24.756
Touché, douché.

05:25.463 --> 05:28.432
- What?
- I said touché, douché.

05:35.139 --> 05:36.629
&lt;i>I really can't stay&lt;/i>

05:37.208 --> 05:39.699
&lt;i>Baby, it's cold outside&lt;/i>

05:39.877 --> 05:41.970
&lt;i>I got to go away&lt;/i>

05:42.146 --> 05:43.943
&lt;i>Baby, it's cold outside&lt;/i>

05:44.115 --> 05:45.946
You mind? I'm trying to sleep.

05:46.117 --> 05:48.381
Hey, I didn't see you there.

05:48.553 --> 05:51.454
- What did you do?
- I don't wanna talk about it.

05:51.622 --> 05:54.455
Fine. I'm not one to pry.

05:57.295 --> 05:59.786
- Money?
- No.

05:59.998 --> 06:02.330
- Old girlfriend?
- No.

06:02.500 --> 06:05.731
- She find those Polaroids?
- No.

06:06.871 --> 06:08.600
How'd you know about the Polaroids?

06:08.773 --> 06:11.674
You just told me, you dirtbag.

06:11.843 --> 06:14.141
So, what did you do?

06:14.312 --> 06:17.839
Try to sneak in at 2 a.m.
Smelling of booze and pole dancer?

06:18.549 --> 06:21.382
For your information,
Chelsea's the one who came home late.

06:21.552 --> 06:23.179
And she was smelling of horse.

06:23.354 --> 06:25.686
Good Lord, Charlie,
you can't compete with a horse.

06:25.857 --> 06:27.415
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

06:27.625 --> 06:30.093
Seriously, I've seen your talliwacker.

06:30.261 --> 06:32.991
You're blessed
but you ain't no Seabiscuit.

06:33.664 --> 06:37.122
When have you seen my... talliwacker?

06:37.301 --> 06:40.930
Oh, I don't know, maybe the nine
or 10 times I found you passed out...

06:41.139 --> 06:44.131
...in your bathtub, holding it
like it was a floatation device.

06:44.308 --> 06:46.708
Oh. I'm sorry about that.

06:46.878 --> 06:48.573
Don't be.

06:56.087 --> 06:58.180
Mmm, boy.

06:58.723 --> 07:03.217
Breakfast, the most important
meal of the day.

07:03.394 --> 07:05.191
Three scrambled egg whites...

07:05.363 --> 07:08.696
...two slices of I Can't Believe
It's Not Buttered rye toast...

07:08.866 --> 07:10.629
...and to flush it through me...

07:10.802 --> 07:14.795
...a piping-hot cup
of freshly ground coffee.

07:16.574 --> 07:18.201
Shut that thing off.

07:46.404 --> 07:48.702
So decaf?

07:52.110 --> 07:56.410
- Don't push me. I'm not in the mood.
- Did you sleep on the couch last night?

07:56.581 --> 07:59.277
- What's it to you?
- Oh, Charlie, what'd you do?

07:59.450 --> 08:01.441
- Nothing.
- Nothing?

08:01.619 --> 08:07.580
I may have compared Brad's recently
deceased wife to a ball-chasing dog.

08:08.326 --> 08:09.850
Whose balls?

08:10.761 --> 08:14.527
Tennis balls.
Get your mind out of the gutter.

08:14.699 --> 08:17.691
All right, while this is
admittedly a bump in the road...

08:17.869 --> 08:21.600
...you do have an opportunity here to
improve your relationship with Chelsea.

08:21.772 --> 08:22.796
How do you figure?

08:22.974 --> 08:25.636
Think about it. The reason
you're threatened by Brad...

08:25.810 --> 08:28.244
...is because
he's a much better man than you.

08:30.014 --> 08:34.041
No, he's not. I would never come on
to another guy's fiancée.

08:34.218 --> 08:36.652
First, we don't know that
he's come on to Chelsea.

08:36.821 --> 08:40.120
Secondly, I've seen you hit on
a bride walking down the aisle.

08:40.858 --> 08:44.794
That was a joke. I asked her what she
was doing later. Everybody laughed.

08:44.962 --> 08:47.692
My point is, if Chelsea's looking
for a better guy...

08:47.865 --> 08:49.799
...why not make that guy you?

08:50.301 --> 08:53.429
Because I'm not a better guy than me.

08:53.604 --> 08:57.438
Not yet. But you do have something
going for you that Brad doesn't.

08:57.608 --> 09:00.577
- What's that?
- Room to improve.

09:02.446 --> 09:05.973
Lots and lots of room to improve.

09:06.150 --> 09:08.641
Thanks, you've filled me
with optimism.

09:08.819 --> 09:11.947
Keep in mind, you're the underdog.
Everybody loves an underdog.

09:12.690 --> 09:15.318
Then how come nobody loves you?

09:17.195 --> 09:20.358
The principle is still sound.
Just go up there and tell Chelsea...

09:20.531 --> 09:24.763
...you know you're a flawed human,
but you'll spend the rest of your life...

09:24.936 --> 09:27.928
...trying to be better
because she deserves the best.

09:29.006 --> 09:31.031
So lie.

09:31.209 --> 09:33.871
Don't lie. Don't you think
you're a flawed human being?

09:34.045 --> 09:37.708
Of course I do. But I know me.
I'm not gonna spend the rest of my life...

09:37.882 --> 09:40.976
...doing anything, let alone trying
to be a better human being.

09:41.152 --> 09:42.449
Oh, come on, Charlie.

09:42.620 --> 09:45.248
Look at every New Year's resolution
I've ever made.

09:45.423 --> 09:48.392
I've got the best of intentions,
but by January 3rd or 4th...

09:48.559 --> 09:52.290
...there I am: Broke, hung-over
and coughing up stripper glitter.

09:52.863 --> 09:54.330
Okay, lie.

09:59.070 --> 10:02.233
Hey, Chels, I brought you
some orange juice.

10:02.907 --> 10:04.875
Thank you. Is there any coffee?

10:05.042 --> 10:08.637
No, no, my stupid brother
broke the grinder.

10:11.549 --> 10:13.676
There's vodka in this orange juice.

10:14.218 --> 10:16.812
Whoopsie, that's mine.

10:17.421 --> 10:19.321
It's 8:00 in the morning.

10:19.490 --> 10:21.151
Hence the orange juice.

10:24.128 --> 10:29.293
So listen, I wanted to apologize again
about my unfortunate remarks last night.

10:29.467 --> 10:32.561
And tell you I love you and
I'll spend the rest of my life...

10:32.737 --> 10:35.672
...trying to be a better man,
because you deserve the best.

10:36.641 --> 10:38.472
Well, I appreciate you saying that.

10:38.643 --> 10:40.270
So...

10:40.511 --> 10:41.569
...we're good?

10:42.580 --> 10:44.070
Yeah.

10:44.248 --> 10:45.374
Great.

10:45.950 --> 10:48.851
What do you wanna do today?
Whatever makes you happy.

10:49.020 --> 10:51.352
- Really?
- I'll go anywhere, I'll do anything.

10:51.522 --> 10:53.456
Of course, you'll have to drive.

10:54.625 --> 10:57.423
I was going to Beverly Hills
for this charity blood drive.

10:57.595 --> 11:01.122
Great. We'll give blood together.
Nothing I like better on a Sunday...

11:01.299 --> 11:03.233
...than tapping a vein
for a good cause.

11:03.768 --> 11:05.759
Terrific. Brad'll be happy to see us.

11:07.004 --> 11:09.234
- Brad?
- It's his charity.

11:10.107 --> 11:13.304
He's got another charity?
What the hell is this guy's problem?

11:14.211 --> 11:17.874
It's not a problem, Charlie.
He's a caring and compassionate man.

11:18.049 --> 11:21.041
Yeah, yeah, yeah,
he's a freaking saint.

11:21.218 --> 11:23.379
And you were planning on
seeing him again.

11:23.554 --> 11:26.318
Well, yeah. He told me about
the blood drive last night.

11:26.490 --> 11:29.323
Right, right, while you were
"cleaning up."

11:29.493 --> 11:30.926
What's "this"?

11:31.095 --> 11:33.620
Oh, I think you know what "this" is.

11:34.899 --> 11:36.161
Just go to hell.

11:36.334 --> 11:40.998
I'm not the one sneaking around, seeing
somebody behind my fiancé's back.

11:41.172 --> 11:43.970
I am not sneaking around.
I asked you to go with me.

11:44.141 --> 11:46.336
Figuring that I wouldn't. Very sneaky.

11:46.510 --> 11:47.738
Drop dead.

11:51.882 --> 11:53.577
Fixed it.

12:05.429 --> 12:06.862
So...

12:08.366 --> 12:11.392
...when are you gonna call Chelsea
and tell her you're sorry?

12:12.470 --> 12:15.837
Okay, first of all,
I have nothing to be sorry about.

12:16.006 --> 12:17.769
I am not gonna discuss my life...

12:17.942 --> 12:20.433
...with someone whose girlfriend
is a gym sock.

12:20.611 --> 12:24.775
Wow, no wonder she left.
You just lash out for no reason.

12:26.350 --> 12:27.510
Hello?

12:27.685 --> 12:30.415
Out here. That's my reason.

12:30.588 --> 12:33.751
Boo-hoo. When are you gonna stop blaming
your problems on your mommy?

12:36.127 --> 12:39.619
Charlie, where's your bride-to-be?
We were gonna finalize the guest list.

12:40.197 --> 12:42.688
- She's not here.
- She told him to go to hell.

12:43.300 --> 12:44.699
Will you please shut up?

12:44.869 --> 12:47.099
Oh, Charles, what did you do?

12:47.271 --> 12:50.434
- I didn't do anything.
- He slept on the couch last night.

12:51.275 --> 12:52.833
Nobody's talking to you.

12:53.277 --> 12:55.802
And this is
what we've been living with.

12:57.014 --> 13:00.506
Stop heating your socks
in the microwave, you little freak.

13:00.684 --> 13:03.619
Charlie, please don't let this girl
get away.

13:03.788 --> 13:05.050
Don't worry, I won't.

13:05.222 --> 13:08.453
Good, because she's one in a million
and you're a dime a dozen.

13:09.827 --> 13:12.728
Yeah, but I'm the underdog
and everybody loves the underdog.

13:12.897 --> 13:15.388
Oh, God, now you sound
like your brother.

13:17.368 --> 13:19.199
How do you plan on getting her back?

13:19.703 --> 13:21.534
I'm gonna become a better man.

13:22.373 --> 13:25.740
Great, so no plan at all.

13:28.913 --> 13:31.848
&lt;i>Later on tonight
it gets windy, even in Southern California.&lt;/i>

13:32.016 --> 13:35.349
&lt;i>By tomorrow, watch those passes
coming down through the Grapevine...&lt;/i>

13:35.519 --> 13:36.816
What's the forecast?

13:37.555 --> 13:40.888
High tonight, low tomorrow.

13:41.058 --> 13:44.755
A hundred percent
chance of hangover.

13:45.262 --> 13:47.253
Heard from Chelsea?

13:47.431 --> 13:50.525
She's staying with her
father for a few days.

13:50.701 --> 13:53.602
At least that's what she e-mailed me.

13:53.771 --> 13:56.205
You don't think she could be with?

13:56.373 --> 14:01.401
Go ahead, say it. Brad.

14:03.781 --> 14:07.239
You know what?
If she is, fine. Good riddance.

14:07.418 --> 14:10.285
I was never meant to be
tied down to one woman anyway.

14:10.454 --> 14:12.319
Well, you are by nature a free spirit.

14:12.490 --> 14:17.052
I miss her, Alan!
I can't live without her!

14:17.228 --> 14:18.422
And you don't have to.

14:18.596 --> 14:20.621
Remember our talk?
Becoming a better man?

14:20.798 --> 14:23.266
Screw it! I'm as good
as I'm ever gonna be!

14:23.434 --> 14:27.632
- Lf she doesn't like it, the hell with her!
- That is true. In a healthy relationship...

14:27.805 --> 14:29.864
...your partner accepts you
for who you are.

14:30.307 --> 14:34.107
Oh, she deserves better
than me, Alan.

14:34.278 --> 14:36.269
She's such a wonderful gal.

14:36.447 --> 14:37.778
I know. I know.

14:37.948 --> 14:41.440
She's like an angel.

14:41.619 --> 14:43.246
She sure is.

14:43.420 --> 14:46.719
Then why is she
running off with Brad?

14:47.691 --> 14:50.319
We don't know that she's
running off with anyone.

14:50.494 --> 14:53.156
This is not angel behavior, Alan.

14:53.330 --> 14:57.323
You know what kind of
behavior this is? Charlie behavior.

14:59.270 --> 15:03.502
I took an angel
and I turned her into me!

15:20.224 --> 15:21.919
Charlie?

15:22.493 --> 15:27.157
I can't sleep in my bed,
it smells like Chelsea.

15:28.232 --> 15:32.828
Okay, well, why don't you stay here...

15:33.003 --> 15:36.871
...and I'll go sleep in your room?
- No, no, no, don't go.

15:38.175 --> 15:40.643
I don't wanna be alone.

15:41.312 --> 15:42.802
All right.

15:44.481 --> 15:47.143
You're wearing
pajama bottoms, right?

15:48.419 --> 15:50.819
Shh.

15:51.755 --> 15:53.882
Exactly how drunk are you?

15:57.494 --> 16:01.726
Both questions asked and answered.

16:13.844 --> 16:15.368
What?

16:16.146 --> 16:18.273
Oh, hi, Chelsea.

16:18.482 --> 16:21.542
No. No, he's up.

16:21.986 --> 16:23.613
Or not.

16:25.756 --> 16:27.724
Hang on, I'll find him.

16:28.392 --> 16:30.019
Charlie?

16:30.694 --> 16:32.218
Charlie?

16:36.634 --> 16:38.226
Found him. Hold on.

16:38.402 --> 16:40.131
Hey, Charlie.

16:41.305 --> 16:42.863
- What?
- You got a phone call.

16:43.040 --> 16:45.372
- I'll call back.
- It's your fiancée.

16:47.945 --> 16:49.879
Oh, hey, baby.

16:50.547 --> 16:53.380
No, no. No, I've been up for a while.

16:54.585 --> 16:56.018
So how are you?

16:56.520 --> 16:57.987
Uh-huh.

16:58.155 --> 16:59.247
What's going on?

16:59.423 --> 17:02.722
Man, you'll do anything not to
kick in a little rent, won't you?

17:04.561 --> 17:07.928
Are you coming home?
I really miss you.

17:08.599 --> 17:12.558
Uh, sure, I can meet you for coffee,
no problem.

17:12.736 --> 17:16.672
Half hour? No problem. See you.

17:18.909 --> 17:20.570
Problem?

17:21.545 --> 17:23.376
What the hell are you doing here?

17:27.084 --> 17:29.279
Hi, sweetie.

17:30.421 --> 17:33.049
- Sorry I'm late.
- I got you some coffee.

17:33.223 --> 17:34.986
Thank you.

17:41.598 --> 17:42.758
Isn't that awfully hot?

17:43.267 --> 17:45.258
Scalding.

17:46.136 --> 17:49.264
Ahh. Whew.

17:49.740 --> 17:53.141
- So, what's new?
- We need to talk about Brad.

17:53.310 --> 17:55.505
No, no, we don't.

17:55.679 --> 18:00.275
I'm sorry. I trust you and I was
totally and completely wrong...

18:00.451 --> 18:02.612
...to think there might be
something going on.

18:03.053 --> 18:06.955
- Thank you for that.
- You're welcome. Okay, let's go home.

18:07.691 --> 18:11.354
Hold on, I do have
a confession to make.

18:11.528 --> 18:13.826
Oh, this is never good.

18:15.866 --> 18:19.802
The reason I got so upset by
the things you said was because...

18:19.970 --> 18:21.301
...you touched a nerve.

18:21.472 --> 18:26.341
Yeah, I do that, I'm a nerve toucher.
Runs in the family.

18:26.510 --> 18:28.034
Okay, well, confession's over.

18:28.212 --> 18:30.646
You forgive me, I forgive you.
Let's go home.

18:31.348 --> 18:34.112
- I'm not done.
- Oh, crap.

18:37.421 --> 18:40.288
The thing is,
I was kind of attracted to Brad.

18:42.392 --> 18:45.520
He's a great guy
and we have a lot in common.

18:45.696 --> 18:50.292
He loves his family and he really cares
about his friends and his community.

18:51.401 --> 18:54.802
I'm taking from your tone
that stuff's important to you.

18:55.439 --> 18:57.373
Yes, Charlie, it's important to me.

18:57.541 --> 18:59.236
Okay.

19:00.344 --> 19:04.007
Did you and Brad do anything
other than talk?

19:04.448 --> 19:06.541
Of course not. Nothing's happened.

19:06.717 --> 19:08.378
Oh, thank God.

19:08.552 --> 19:10.611
But while I do love you...

19:10.788 --> 19:12.983
...I need to know
you care as much as I do.

19:13.157 --> 19:15.455
- I do.
- You say that...

19:15.659 --> 19:18.150
...but are you willing to
work on our relationship?

19:18.328 --> 19:23.095
Of course I am. We can start doing
things together, community things.

19:23.267 --> 19:26.031
You know, with the kids that are poor...

19:26.203 --> 19:29.195
...and the old people
that fall and can't get up.

19:30.440 --> 19:33.170
- What about your family?
- I'll get a new family.

19:34.778 --> 19:39.477
I'm telling you, I can change,
I can be a better man...

19:39.683 --> 19:43.983
...the man you want me to be.
And I promise you...

19:44.188 --> 19:45.917
Excuse me.

19:48.258 --> 19:50.385
- Oh, my God!
- I am so, so sorry.

19:50.561 --> 19:53.052
You threw up on my baby!

19:54.598 --> 19:57.624
Anyway, to be fair,
I don't think the carrots were mine.

19:57.801 --> 19:59.564
Get away from him, you pig!

19:59.736 --> 20:02.102
I'm sorry. I'm sorry.

20:03.574 --> 20:05.439
Cute kid.

20:08.846 --> 20:10.473
Chels?

20:17.721 --> 20:19.450
Damn.

20:31.668 --> 20:34.262
I just got a call from Chelsea.

20:34.871 --> 20:36.566
Oh, yeah?

20:36.740 --> 20:40.073
She said she wants to
postpone the wedding.

20:41.044 --> 20:42.671
I know.

20:43.280 --> 20:45.180
I'm sorry.

20:46.350 --> 20:47.874
Thanks.

20:49.219 --> 20:54.714
Believe it or not, I do love you
and I hate to see you hurt.

20:54.891 --> 20:59.191
Yeah, well, I guess
I kind of had it coming.

20:59.363 --> 21:01.593
But you tried.

21:01.765 --> 21:03.756
I did.

21:05.902 --> 21:07.665
I just have one question.

21:08.639 --> 21:09.731
What's that?

21:09.906 --> 21:11.999
Did you really vomit on a baby?

21:18.315 --> 21:20.715
Don't beat yourself up too much.

21:20.884 --> 21:22.909
We've all done that.

21:23.887 --> 21:25.616
You're kidding.

21:26.623 --> 21:31.390
Of course, most of us
do it on our own babies.
